Bluedroid AG: size CVSD audio packets by the voice setting's sample size, not always 16 bits.

Needed for the Freecom 2x's EV5 CVSD link (180-byte eSCO packets, 22.5 ms). With the default
16-bit linear PCM over HCI, each packet is 360 bytes, more than the 8-bit HCI SCO length field
allows. The ESP32 controller (closed source) keeps only 360 mod 256 = 104 bytes per packet in
both directions, so the link has to use 8-bit samples (u-law, set with `ag esco`, voice
setting 0x0100), which makes each packet 180 bytes. Bluedroid assumed 2 bytes per sample for
CVSD, so it cut the app's audio into 360-byte packets, which BTM_WriteScoData() truncated.

CMakeLists.txt also raises BTM_SCO_DATA_SIZE_MAX (largest HCI SCO packet Bluedroid sends) from
120 to 240 for the 180-byte packets.

Applied to ~/.platformio/packages/framework-espidf by tools/apply_patches.py before each build.

diff --git a/components/bt/host/bluedroid/bta/hf_ag/bta_ag_sco.c b/components/bt/host/bluedroid/bta/hf_ag/bta_ag_sco.c
index e58f462..8d1d9d7 100644
--- a/components/bt/host/bluedroid/bta/hf_ag/bta_ag_sco.c
+++ b/components/bt/host/bluedroid/bta/hf_ag/bta_ag_sco.c
@@ -210,8 +210,15 @@ static void bta_ag_sco_conn_cback(UINT16 sco_idx)
 
         if (sco_data.air_mode == BTM_SCO_AIR_MODE_CVSD)
         {
-            p_scb->out_pkt_len = sco_data.tx_pkt_len * 2;
-            p_scb->in_pkt_len = sco_data.rx_pkt_len * 2;
+            /* open-intercom: bytes per sample over HCI follow the voice setting the link was set
+               up with (bta_ag_create_sco and bta_ag_sco_conn_rsp use the same params): 2 for
+               16-bit linear PCM, 1 for 8-bit linear, u-law or A-law. Was always 2. */
+            UINT16 voice = bta_ag_cb.sco.param_updated ? bta_ag_cb.sco.params.voice_contfmt
+                                                       : BTM_VOICE_SETTING_CVSD;
+            UINT16 bytes_per_sample = ((voice & HCI_INP_CODING_MASK) == HCI_INP_CODING_LINEAR &&
+                                       (voice & HCI_INP_SAMPLE_SIZE_MASK) == HCI_INP_SAMPLE_SIZE_16BIT) ? 2 : 1;
+            p_scb->out_pkt_len = sco_data.tx_pkt_len * bytes_per_sample;
+            p_scb->in_pkt_len = sco_data.rx_pkt_len * bytes_per_sample;
         }
         else {
             p_scb->out_pkt_len = sco_data.tx_pkt_len;
